WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.937
"How to Boost Collagen Synthesis with Diet"

00:00:10.129 --> 00:00:13.140
As we age, the synthesis
of collagen decreases

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.580
by about 1 percent a year,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.700
which may contribute
to the development of wrinkles.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.560
Though we don't have evidence

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.220
that collagen is superior to any
other proteins for aging skin,

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.880
those who do want to try it
are advised to contact

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.120
the manufacturers
to clarify its source.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.180
Most collagen supplements don't
disclose this information

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.680
and for good reason.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.980
Terrestrial sources
can include a witch's brew

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.340
of kangaroo and rat tails,
duck feet, horse tendons,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.140
alligator bones,
and frog skin.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.220
Aquatic sources are mainly
from fish skins, bones, heads,

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.900
scales, fins, and entrails.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.600
Recommended questions
for manufacturers include

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.640
"What measures were used
to protect against

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.920
contamination or adulteration?

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.120
If sourced from fish,
were low-mercury fish used?

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.860
If sourced from cows,

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.080
what steps were taken
to ensure that

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.360
no brain or nervous system
matter was included,

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.520
in order to prevent
prion disease?"

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.960
In the United States,

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.380
collagen is exempt
from FDA prohibitions

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.900
against using risky tissues
like brains--

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.960
prohibitions in place
to protect consumers

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.540
against bovine spongiform
encephalopathy,

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.700
also known as mad cow disease.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.000
So, for food safety,
religious, ethical,

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.800
or allergy-related reasons,

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.740
there have been calls
for non-animal alternatives.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.020
For example, 2 to 4 percent
of the population

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.180
is allergic to bovine collagen.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.120
To solve the mad cow conundrum,

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.160
there have been calls
to genetically engineer

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.420
cattle without prions

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.660
to "offer a safe source
of collagen-based materials."

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.480
But why not just get
plants to make it?

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.500
A technique has been perfected
to produce collagen from plants,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.260
but it has not yet reached
commercial viability.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.160
It's hard to beat
the cost of feet.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:04.860
But what about all of the vegan
collagen products on the market?

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.200
If you look closely,
you'll see the small print:

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.340
vegan collagen builder
or vegan collagen booster.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.200
It's not actually collagen,

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.180
since collagen
is made by animals,

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.180
but you're an animal,
you make collagen.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.200
So they're suggesting

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.940
their supplements
can boost production,

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.680
but since it appears

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.600
none of them have actually
been put to the test,

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.340
I assume it's all
a load of bunk.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.320
But there are some
foods and nutrients

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.940
that have been investigated.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:35.280
Researchers burned the butts
of 20 women with a UV lamp

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.660
before and after half of them

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.420
ate three tablespoons
of tomato paste each day

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.560
for three months.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.100
And there was a significant
reduction in MMP-1 levels

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.740
in the derrieres of those
who had been randomized

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.000
to the tomatoes.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.700
(That's a major
collagen-eating enzyme

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.220
that plays a role in skin aging
caused by the sun.)

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.240
Butt biopsies also show
that the amount of beta-carotene

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.920
found in about
one and a third cup

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.140
of sweet potato
can boost collagen production

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.600
as much as four-fold
within three months.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.300
To test the effects of greens,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.400
Korean researchers
randomized older women

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.620
to the amount of chlorophyll
found in a few tablespoons

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:11.760
of cooked spinach a day.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.400
After three months,
skin biopsies showed

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.680
a significant increase
in collagen production,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.200
accompanied by an increase
in skin elasticity

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.320
and a decrease
in facial wrinkles.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.920
Unfortunately, this was just
a before-and-after comparison

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.320
to baseline study
with no control group,

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.700
but there have been

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.500
placebo-controlled
randomized trials,

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.540
and of kale no less!

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.620
Compared to placebo, there was
a significant improvement

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.020
in a noninvasive measure
of skin collagen status

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.000
after 10 months
of being randomized

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.560
to an extract of curly kale.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.860
The researchers concluded
that "a healthy lifestyle

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.840
including a diet
rich in carotenoids

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.280
is the best prevention strategy

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.740
against premature skin aging."

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.380
That led to dermatology
journal commentaries

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.840
with titles like "Eat plenty
of green leafy vegetables

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.660
for protection from
the pro-aging rays of the sun,"

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.660
but might it actually be
more than that?

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:07.380
Sulforaphane, the cruciferous
compound in kale and broccoli,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.600
may be able to mobilize
cellular defenses

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.300
that protect skin
against damage by UV radiation,

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.940
as well as mitigate
the premature skin aging

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.160
induced by air pollution
particulate matter,

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.760
though this was on skin cells
in a Petri dish.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.240
Soybean compounds can increase
collagen deposition

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.260
and prevent wrinkles in mice,
but what about in people?

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.720
Given improvements
of skin aging

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.880
seen with menopausal
hormone therapy

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.500
but concerned
about the side effects,

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.620
researchers in Brazil
tried giving phytohormones,

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:40.560
plant hormones in the form
of soy phytoestrogens.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.360
Twenty-nine
postmenopausal women

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.880
were given the amount
in four servings a day

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.500
of soy foods for six months.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.140
Unfortunately,
there was no control group,

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.600
but they did take skin biopsies
before and after

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.480
and found a significant
improvement in skin thickness,

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.400
along with increased
collagen content

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.420
and elastic fibers.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:00.180
The biopsies
of 25 out of 29 women

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.220
showed an increase in collagen.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.340
You could also throw in
some vitamin C-rich foods,

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.920
as vitamin C appears
to stimulate collagen production

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.180
from human skin cells.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.600
Defective wound healing
has long been known

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.640
as a major manifestation
of scurvy,

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.440
the vitamin C-deficiency
disease.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:20.100
In fact, a remarkable series
of grisly experiments

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.500
performed on British
conscientious objectors

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.520
during World War II

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:26.520
involved being subjected
to cuts and stab wounds

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.320
after being randomized
to different levels

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.280
of vitamin C.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:30.720
The researchers found

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.580
that the average
daily vitamin C intake

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:36.360
to prevent weak scar formation
was about 95 milligrams,

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:38.880
which is actually higher than
the current recommendations

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:42.960
but nothing you can't get
from half a bell pepper.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.960
Vitamin B12 also appears
to be necessary

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:47.940
for maximum collagen synthesis,

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:50.580
which may explain why
collagen synthesis rates

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.400
appear to be about 10 percent
lower in vegetarians,

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.500
because the prevalence
of B12 deficiency

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.740
among those eating
plant-based diets is so high.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.920
That's one of many reasons
why it's critically important

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.320
that everyone consuming
a plant-based diet

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:08.220
ensures a regular, reliable
source of vitamin B12.

